Z||000013||WhiteFieroBlur||11-01-2001||01:28 AM||||Ok lets see am I addicted? <BR>  I woke up all day I spent playing on my computer and looking on the forum till I went to work. Now I just got off of work and suppose to be going to a party so instead I run inside and turned on my computer and shoot right here. Hmm I will be on here for a few hours and goto bed and get up in the morning and go right back here till I goto work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P> But I am not addicted I don't think. but what is true is that this place is like wonderfull. I have recently been lookin online for some fiero boards and nothing compares to the members and info we have here. I mean you can live off of this stuff for the rest of your life about your fiero. I think we have posted so many times that we are going around in circles with the same topics. This place also makes you drool, ya'll have some pretty nice lookin fieros, one day I hope to be in a show with mine but I think not. I just wish I lived near some of ya'll to visit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cliff Pennock||11-01-2001||05:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by x-thumpr-x:<BR><B>"YOU spend more time on that computer then ME!"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I laughed so hard when I read that! Then I realized it said "then ME" and <I>not</I> "then <B>on</B> ME".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Sorry 'bout that...||||reg||1
Z||000015||Sage||11-01-2001||06:57 AM||||Cliff;<P>I read it the same way!  Then also came to the same realization.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>As for being addicted...can you say "Fiero Fix"?<P>Talking to others who don't know, or aren't involved is problematic, as you want to say "on the forum" but you see that "look" that reflects the thought, "what is he talkin about?"  but they usually just nod and change the subject, or say "What's that"<P>LOL<BR>As for the girlfriend thing...it's just a thing some girls,(people) have.  Some of them just want to be the center of your world, all the time.  Don't do it though!  If you do, they will chaulk it up as a "victory" and get bored and tend to move on to the next challenge.  Before my wife and I were married, she would get agitated if I read a book!  (This was before PC's)  She was verrry young at the time, so most of them will out grow it given enough time.  Oh BTW, I have read many books since then!  If it becomes a problem, try getting her involved with what you are doing, or get involved, or at least show an interest in what she does.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||1
